Third-party material

This repository cites material property values, test-standard requirements and references from other publishers. They are not Anisotropy's: each keeps its owner's terms, and LICENSE grants nothing in them. Every source the materials library cites carries one of these rights classes (lib/source-rights.ts, ADR-0018):

- Public domain: free of copyright, for example a US government work such as MIL-HDBK-17-2F. Values may be shown and a copy may be hosted.
- Open publisher: distributed publicly by its publisher, for example NCAMP qualification reports, NASA technical reports and manufacturer datasheets. Values are shown with their citation and a link to the publisher's copy; the documents are not copied here.
- Licensed reference: a copyrighted work, for example a textbook, CMH-17 or an ASTM test standard. Only individual values are recorded, each cited by its table and page or its clause; no scans, extracted text, tables, figures or PDFs are published, and readers are directed to their own copy.

Each record names its source, its rights class and the evidence for that class: lib/curated-materials.ts, lib/qualification-materials.ts, lib/qualification-references.json, lib/textbook-source.ts and lib/source-rights.ts.

Marks and media of others

The site names The Basement at UC San Diego, the Launchpad cohort the team is part of, in words; it shows no mark of theirs until written permission is recorded (ADR-0081 amendment 2). Names and marks of other organisations keep their owners' terms, and LICENSE grants nothing in them. Photographs and other media owned by someone other than Anisotropy keep their owners' terms in the same way.

